A thread has time with less than a tick in its account.
It would take turns on the run queue it cannot pay for, before the threads on spare time;
a thread has time exactly while its account holds a tick.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its account says
Report: a tick did not cost the thread whose turn it was a tick less its units
Report: the timer lets a tick pass that ends the turn
Report: the timer lets the tick pass that drains the turn's account
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-earns

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@ static inline void account_refill(struct place *p)
